From 88cbfbb0eba9793d5ca4d224271c27418e54caf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:11:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.8a: Bandwidth Limiter on the QoS page +
 language-selector fixes (both variants)

Fold the stock per-device Bandwidth Limiter into the Reaper QoS page: the Bandwidth
Limiter mode now has an on-page editor (device/MAC + download/upload Mb/s, enable/remove,
32-device cap) that reads/writes qos_bw_rulelist in the exact stock format and applies
through the existing QoS flow. Hide QoS_EZQoS.asp from the menu (menuTree.js) and redirect
any direct/framed hit to Reaper_QoS.asp (reaper_inject.c SUP map). Remove the crimson
"editor" link from that mode card.

Language-selector fixes from v1.4.8 on-hardware testing:
- Include the current language in the topbar dropdown (shown_language_css omits it) so you
  can switch back to English and the active language shows as selected.
- Make the selector more visible (globe icon, crimson border, brighter text).
- Clean the Traffic_Analyzer dict value in the 5 languages that shipped it as "English +
  native" (CN/TW/CZ/KR/NL) so the side-nav label replaces instead of appends; add nav-label
  ellipsis + a dashboard overflow-x guard so no language can force a horizontal scrollbar.

6 new dict keys (RQOS_110-115) added to all 25 dict files. www + one httpd source file
(reaper_inject.c); both images (MCP + noMCP) built and validated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
